{"strongs": "H3034", "word": "יָדָה", "translit": "ya.dah", "root": "ידד", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "throw, cast", "definition": "[ יָדָה ] verb throw, cast (Arabic exeruit, emisit , II. IV. emisit (all now in special senses); Ethiopic throw, cast on or in (very often; compare ); where Hiph`il give thanks, confess (originally acknowledge ?) is commonly derived, perhaps from gestures accompanying the act, see Thes Lag Or. ii. 22 , yet connection uncertain; Aramaic Pa`el וַדֵּי , Aph`el אוֺדִּי confess , , id. ; but Ethiopic accuse , perhaps also from gesture; Palmyrene מודא render thanks , often in votive inscriptions, see Vog on No. 79; עבד ומודא Vog No. 101 = εὐχαρίστως ἀνέθηκε ; מודן כל יום Vog No. 93. 1 ; ** Palmyrene ידתא pious , read ירתא נה ) SAC 80 also Id JQ 1904, 593 . ידתא pious Vog No. 29 ) — Qal Imperative יְדוּ אֶלֿ shoot (arrows) at Jer 50:14 (read probably, with some Manuscripts יְרוּ ). Pi`el Imperfect וַיַּדּוּ בִּי Lam 3:53 and they cast (stones) on me; Infinitive יַדּוֺת Zech 2:4 to cast down (the horns of the nations). Hiph`il (connection with ידה throw , obscure, yet see above) Perfect הוֺדוּ 1Kgs 8:33 + 3 t.; הוֺדִינוּ Ps 75:2 (twice in verse); Imperfect יְהוֺדֶה Neh 11:17 (on form see Ges «GKC:53»§ 53 , R. 7); יוֺדֶה Ps 6:6 1 singular suffix אֲהוֺדֶנּוּ Ps 28:7 ( Ges l.c .); אוֺדֶנּוּ Ps 42:6 ; Ps 42:12 ; Ps 43:5 plural יוֺדוּ Ps 99:3 + 6 t.; suffix יְהוֺדוּךָ Ps 45:18 ( Ges l.c .); יוֺדֻךָ Ps 49:19 , etc. + 41 t. Imperfect; Imperative הוֺדוּ Isa 12:4 + 16 t.; הֹדוּ Ps 107:1 Infinitive הוֺדוֺת 1Chr 25:3 + 11 t.; הוֺדֹת Ezra 3:11 הֹדוֺת 1Chr 16:7 + 4 t. (see. Baer Ps 92:2 ); Participle מוֺדֶה Prov 28:13 plural מוֺדִים 1Chr 29:13 — 1. give thanks, laud, praise ; \\ \\ a. with accusative (1) of men, Judah Gen 49:8 (poetic play on name); Job (ironical) Job 40:14 the king Ps 45:18 the rich Ps 49:19 (2) of ׳ י , Gen 29:35 ( J explanation name יהודה ); elsewhere (mostly Psalms and Chronicles) of ritual worship (see Lag Or. ii. 22 f. ); object ׳ שֵׁם בי Isa 25:1 ; Ps 44:9 ; Ps 54:8 ; Ps 99:3 ; Ps 138:2 ; Ps 142:8 ׳ פֶּלֶא י Ps 89:6 יהוה Ps 7:18 ; Ps 9:2 ; Ps 109:30 ; Ps 111:1 יָהּ Ps 118:10 suffix ךָ - referring to God Ps 30:10 ; Ps 30:13 ; Ps 35:18 ; Ps 43:4 ; Ps 52:11 ; Ps 67:4 (twice in verse); Ps 67:6 (twice in verse); Ps 71:22 ; Ps 76:11 ; Ps 88:11 ; Ps 118:21 ; Ps 118:28 ; Ps 119:7 ; Ps 138:1 ; Ps 139:14 ; Isa 38:18 ; Isa 38:19 (song of Hezekiah); — נֶּ֯וּ Ps 42:6 ; Ps 42:12 ; Ps 43:5 מִשִּׁירִי אֲהוֺדֶנּוּ Ps 28:7 with my song will I praise him ; ׳ אוֺדְךָ י I will praise thee ׳ י 2Sam 22:50 = Ps 18:50 = Ps 108:4 , Isa 12:1 (exilic hymn); אדני Ps 57:10 ; Ps 86:12 , compare Ps 138:4 ; Ps 145:10 . \\ \\ b. followed by לְ only of the ritual worship: ׳ לְשֵׁם י Ps 106:47 = 1Chr 16:35 ; Ps 122:4 ; Ps 140:14 לְזֵכֶר קָדְשׁוֺ Ps 30:5 ; Ps 97:12 ׳ לי 1Chr 16:4 ; 1Chr 16:7 ; 1Chr 16:41 ; 1Chr 23:30 ; 1Chr 25:3 ; 2Chr 5:13 ; 2Chr 7:6 ; 2Chr 20:22 ; Ps 33:2 ; Ps 92:2 ; Ps 105:1 = 1Chr 16:8 = Isa 12:4 כי טוב ׳ הודו לי give thanks to ׳ י for he is good Ps 106:1 ; Ps 107:1 ; Ps 118:1 ; Ps 118:29 ; Ps 136:1 ; 1Chr 16:34 so Jer 33:11 (followed by ׳ אֶתיֿ ); compare הוד(ו)ת 2Chr 7:3 ; Ezra 3:11 חסדו ׳ יודו לי Ps 107:8 ; Ps 107:15 ; Ps 107:21 ; Ps 107:31 לאלהים Neh 12:46 ; Ps 136:1 לאדני v Ps 136:3 לאל v Ps 136:26 suffixes referring to God: לְךָ Ps 6:6 ; Ps 79:13 ; Ps 119:62 לוֺ Ps 100:4 לך + אלהים Ps 75:2 (twice in verse); 1Chr 29:13 absolute 2Chr 31:2 ; Neh 11:17 ; Neh 12:24 all of the ritual worship. 2. confess , \\ \\ a. the name of God, || שׁוּב , התחנן , התפלל , 1Kgs 8:33 ; 1Kgs 8:35 = 2Chr 6:24 ; 2Chr 6:26 . \\ \\ b. עֲלֵי פשׁע Ps 32:5 (|| לֹא כִסִּיתִי ); (פשׁעיו) מוֺדֶה וְעֹזֵב Prov 28:13 confessing and forsaking (his transgressions; opposed to מְכַסֶּה ). Hithpa`el Perfect הִתְוַדָּה Lev 5:5 ; Lev 16:21 הִתְוַדּוּ Lev 26:40 ; Num 5:7 Imperfect 1 singular אֶתְוַדֶּה Dan 9:4 plural יִתְוַדּוּ Neh 9:2 Infinitive suffix הִתְוַדֹּתוֺ Ezra 10:1 Participle מִתְוַדֶּה Neh 1:6 ; Dan 9:20 plural מִתְוַדִּים 2Chr 30:22 ; Neh 9:3 — 1. confess , absolute Ezra 10:1 ; Neh 9:3 ; Dan 9:4 with accusative עָוֺן Lev 16:21 ( P ), Lev 26:40 ( H ); חטאת Num 5:7 ( P ), Dan 9:20 אֲשֶׁר חָטָא Lev 5:5 ( P ); עַל חטאות Neh 1:6 ; Neh 9:2 . 2. give thanks , ליהוה , in the ritual worship 2Chr 30:22 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3448')\">BDB3448</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3034')\">H3034</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3447')\">BDB3447</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3449')\">BDB3449</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>יָדָה</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>throw, cast</highlightword> (Arabic <placeholder2180/> <highlight>exeruit, emisit</highlight>, II. IV. <highlight>emisit</highlight> (all now in special senses); Ethiopic <placeholder2181/> <highlight>throw, cast</highlight> on or in (very often; compare <placeholder2182/>); where <b>Hiph`il</b> <highlight>give thanks, confess</highlight> (originally <highlight>acknowledge</highlight> ?) is commonly derived, perhaps from gestures accompanying the act, see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Thes')\">Thes</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Lag')\">Lag<sup>Or. ii. 22</sup></lookup>, yet connection uncertain; Aramaic Pa`el <bdbheb>וַדֵּי</bdbheb>, Aph`el <bdbheb>אוֺדִּי</bdbheb> <highlight>confess</highlight>, <placeholder2183/>, <placeholder2184/> <highlight>id.</highlight>; but Ethiopic <placeholder2185/> <highlight>accuse</highlight>, perhaps also from gesture; Palmyrene <bdbheb>מודא</bdbheb> <highlight>render thanks</highlight>, often in votive inscriptions, see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vog')\">Vog</lookup> on No. 79; <bdbheb>עבד ומודא</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vog')\">Vog<sup>No. 101</sup></lookup> = <grk>εὐχαρίστως ἀνέθηκε</grk>; <bdbheb>מודן כל יום</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vog')\">Vog<sup>No. 93. 1</sup></lookup>; <div class=\"remarks\"><b>**</b>Palmyrene <bdbheb>ידתא</bdbheb> <highlight>pious</highlight>, read <bdbheb>ירתא</bdbheb> <bdbheb>נה</bdbheb>) SAC<sup>80</sup> also Id<sup>JQ 1904, 593</sup>. <bdbheb>ידתא</bdbheb> <highlight>pious</highlight> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vog')\">Vog<sup>No. 29</sup></lookup>) — </div><div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Imperative</highlight> <bdbheb>יְדוּ אֶלֿ</bdbheb> <highlight>shoot</highlight> (arrows) <highlight>at</highlight> <ref ref=\"Jer 50:14\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"50\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"50\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(24,50,14)\">Jer 50:14</ref> (read probably, with some Manuscripts <bdbheb>יְרוּ</bdbheb>). <b>Pi`el</b> <highlight>Imperfect</highlight> <bdbheb>וַיַּדּוּ בִּי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lam 3:53\" b=\"25\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"53\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"53\" onclick=\"bcv(25,3,53)\">Lam 3:53</ref> <highlight>and they cast</highlight> (stones) <highlight>on me; Infinitive</highlight> <bdbheb>יַדּוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Zech 2:4\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(38,2,4)\">Zech 2:4</ref> <highlight>to cast down</highlight> (the horns of the nations).</p></div><div class=\"section\"><p><b>Hiph`il</b> (connection with <bdbheb>ידה</bdbheb> <highlight>throw</highlight>, obscure, yet see above) <highlight>Perfect</highlight> <bdbheb>הוֺדוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 8:33\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"33\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"33\" onclick=\"bcv(11,8,33)\">1Kgs 8:33</ref> + 3 t.; <bdbheb>הוֺדִינוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 75:2\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"75\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"75\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(19,75,2)\">Ps 75:2</ref> (twice in verse); <highlight>Imperfect</highlight> <bdbheb>יְהוֺדֶה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Neh 11:17\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(16,11,17)\">Neh 11:17</ref> (on form see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup><sup>«GKC:53»§ 53</sup>, R. 7); <bdbheb>יוֺדֶה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 6:6\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(19,6,6)\">Ps 6:6</ref> 1 singular suffix <bdbheb>אֲהוֺדֶנּוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 28:7\" b=\"1